<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sumatra Treaty</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1871</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Anglo-Dutch Treaty of 1871</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sumatra">Sumatra</a> Treaty was an agreement signed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a> in November 1871. Britain dropped its objection to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> expansion in northern Sumatra, which the treaty of 1824 had limited by recognising <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aceh">Aceh</a>'s independence, in return for equal trading rights there; a linked treaty transferred the Dutch <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gold-coast">Gold Coast</a> to Britain. It cleared the way for the Dutch attack on Aceh in 1873.</p></div>
